PTX CoWW+remote-store+async-bulk.cluster
"P0 in CTA 0 stores 1 to d in CTA 1's shared memory (st.shared::cluster), then copies g (2) into d with cp.async.bulk. The copy's implicit proxy fence is in P0's CTA, and a proxy fence orders only operations in its own thread block (8.9.5); with the write to d by CTA 1 (D21) nothing orders the two stores, so d may end at 1: allowed."
{
d=0 @cta 1;
b=mbarrier(1) @cta 1;
g=2;
}
 P0@cta 0,cluster 0,gpu 0                                                  | P1@cta 1,cluster 0,gpu 0 ;
 st.weak.shared::cluster d, 1                                              |                          ;
 cp.async.bulk.shared::cluster.global.mbarrier::complete_tx::bytes d, g, b |                          ;
exists
(d == 1)
